<p>I think there's a misunderstanding here&#8212;not all reviewers are moderators, and not all moderators are reviewers.</p>
<p>Since one of the main complaints we noted from reviewers was that authors would often ignore feedback unless they asked for it specifically, there was an attempt to shift focus towards authors reaching out to reviewers first to both familiarize themselves with how to ask/whom to ask, as well as confirming that there was an interest in continuing with the idea, rather than making the thread and then never responding to it.</p>
<p>It's true that you shouldn't need to message mods specifically, but reviewers can always be contacted when you're seeking a review.</p>

