<p>Hey, brought in by request so lets see what we have.</p>
<p>Let's look at the SCP itself first. It seems like a fairly interesting concept with how his spirit lives on through the backpack and then imprints upon whomever opens it. But how do we know about the properties of the SCP if it was never tested? More so, is there any reason people keep buying a used backpack? Especially if the SCP dies with it on at the end of it, the backpack could be submitted to police evidence, destroyed, thrown in the garbage, or just never to be found. I would figure out a way to cover this plot hole that you have so that it's better understood how it gets passed on.</p>
<p>As for the Narrative, I have to echo what is said above. This definitely seems more suited for a tale as there is no mention of the Foundation involved. Rather you focus on the SCP itself and its journey, instead of how its contained. This would allow more creativity in terms of how you write the article and express the emotions of the SCP itself. It would also help explain how we know all these details about the SCP despite it not being in Foundation custody. I would suggest a tale either in the form of journal entries or just from the perspective of the SCP itself for what you have. Otherwise, this needs a serious overhaul to make it match an article. Best of luck.</p>

