<p>Welcome to the wonderful world of 400 or less ;-). Read: There is plenty of Foundation involvement and a lot of the plot holes have been covered. Just not in the version presented due to space limits.</p>
<p>1) It's a fairly stout backpack. Definitely worth the $10 in a second-hand store. And that assumes someone doesn't keep it for themselves when they find it. Also, as the body evaporates, there's no crime scene; that also gives it the appearance of an abandoned backpack after a death. As Page rarely dies in a secluded area, it's usually not long before someone finds it.</p>
<p>2) The Foundation had it for a while, but it was &quot;released&quot; when it was grabbed in a GOC raid. One raider kept it just a little too long. The Foundation tries to grab it when it pops up, and a couple of Foundation agents have been lost to the backpack because they ignored parts of the containment process. Thus. while it's easy to track via the IP address of wherever Page logs in, they can't always send someone to retrieve it, especially as they need to do so in less than an hour.</p>
<p>The backpack always creates debates with site admins: Keep in mind that it represents a being with 50 years of life experience who has acquired a wide variety of skills.</p>
<p>3) I'm already looking into the Tales&#8230;.</p>

