<blockquote>
<p>Welcome to the wonderful world of 400 or less ;-). Read: There is plenty of Foundation involvement and a lot of the plot holes have been covered. Just not in the version presented due to space limits.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If you're having difficulty presenting a concept within the wordcount limit, consider the advice from this thread: <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13369776/how-do-i-remain-brief-when-writing-an-scp-concept">http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13369776/how-do-i-remain-brief-when-writing-an-scp-concept</a></p>
<p>ETA: for the record, telling a reviewer &quot;the plot holes are covered, just not where you would see it&quot; doesn't really encourage them to give greenlights. Remember that at the start reviewers have no immediate investment in your concept; it's a bit nonsensical to ask them to give the benefit of the doubt because of the wordcount.</p>

